### API TESTING FILE
### Use with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (click "Send Request"),
### or copy the requests into Postman / Thunder Client.
### Run the server first: npm run server

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### 1. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Register (the first user becomes admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Admin User",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 3. Login  (copy the token from the response and paste it below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 4. Submit a bug report like the widget does (PUBLIC - no token needed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/issues/public
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "bug",
  "title": "Checkout button not working",
  "description": "When I click the checkout button nothing happens and I see an error in the console.",
  "reporterName": "Test Visitor",
  "reporterEmail": "visitor@example.com",
  "pageInfo": {
    "url": "https://example.com/cart",
    "title": "Cart",
    "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0 (test)",
    "screen": "1920x1080",
    "viewport": "1280x720",
    "language": "en-US"
  }
}

### 5. Submit a similar report (AI should flag it as a duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/issues/public
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "bug",
  "description": "Checkout button is not working, clicking it does nothing."
}

### 6. Submit a feature request
POST {{baseUrl}}/issues/public
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "feature",
  "description": "It would be great to have a dark mode option on the website."
}

### ---- PROTECTED ROUTES: replace TOKEN with the token from step 3 ----

### 7. Dashboard stats
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues/stats
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 8. List issues (with filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues?status=open&type=bug&sort=votes
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 9. Team members
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 10. Get one issue (replace ISSUE_ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues/ISSUE_ID
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 11. Update status and assign (replace ISSUE_ID and USER_ID)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/issues/ISSUE_ID
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in-progress",
  "assignedTo": "USER_ID"
}

### 12. Vote / un-vote (toggle)
POST {{baseUrl}}/issues/ISSUE_ID/vote
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 13. Delete (admin only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/issues/ISSUE_ID
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### 14. Negative test: no token should give 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/issues
